    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1655">

                <pb facs="1056" n="940" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg940"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/2325.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President of Nicaragua to the Minister of
                        Nicaragua.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1655-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Intendant of Bluefields has informed me that last night at twelve o’clock the
                    main barracks were attacked by Clifford D. Sands who has been absent from the
                    country. For this reason and in view of other information it is believed that
                    this movement is the work of the enemies of the Convention in order to prevent
                    its approval. The attacking party repelled, Sands took refuge in the American
                    Consulate. Four wounded on our side. Among papers captured there was found a
                    proclamation for the independence of the Coast. All quiet.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Díaz</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1655-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1655-f1-content">
                <p>Handed by the Minister to the Department on July 6, 1914. The convention referred
                    to is the canal treaty of Feb. 8, 1913; see <ref target="frus1913#pg_1021">For.
                        Rel. 1913, pp. 1021</ref>–<ref target="frus1913#pg_1022">1022</ref>
                    (footnote).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
